# WHAT EACH DOCUMENT SAYS ABOUT ITSELF. One row per loaded document: the root element it
# declares, the namespace that element is in, the URN it claims, and -- from the assertion
# roots -- who witnessed it and when.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THE FIRST RELATION IN THIS TREE THAT READS A ROOT ELEMENT. Every other query reaches
#    past it with the descendant axis, because `//pm:stack/pm:layer` finds a stack whether it
#    sits at the root or one level down inside a composition. That is the right shape for
#    asking about a LAYER and the wrong shape for asking about a DOCUMENT, which is how
#    `filing.kind` ends up a substring match on a namespace PREFIX. A prefix is the sender's
#    lexical choice; `local-name()` and `namespace-uri()` are the document's own.
#
# ⛔⛔ THE EMPTY COLUMN IS THE FINDING. Five roots are declared across the two schemas, every
#    `asrt:` one names a witness, and `pm:processModulus` is the only one that does not. A
#    filing says WHICH document it is -- S-28 gave it that -- and then stops. Every fact
#    inside it carries a `pm:Provenance`; the document carries none, so a stipulation and an
#    observation are the same shape to anything reading the tree.
#
# ⛔ `observedAt` AND `ranAt` ARE LEFT AS TWO COLUMNS ON PURPOSE. They are the same question
#   under two spellings and `asrt:coverage` asks it under neither, so a reader can see three
#   roots owing a date answer it three different ways. Folding them with a `coalesce` would
#   assert an equivalence no schema states -- the same reason `week` and `semana` stay apart
#   in units/denominators.sqlc.
#
# ✅⭐⭐ `evidence` IS FILED NOW, AND THIS RELATION IS WHY IT COULD BE ASKED FOR. Writing the
#    query is what made the gap visible: a column for what each document says about itself,
#    with the one fact that decides whether a number may be quoted missing from it. Until 0.4
#    ingest matched `A STIPULATION, NOT A FILING` as a substring over the whole serialised
#    body -- English-only in a repository with a Portuguese edition, and true of any corpus
#    document that merely QUOTED the sentence.
#
# ⛔ THE OTHER TWO PLACES A STIPULATION ANNOUNCES ITSELF, WHICH NOTHING READS AND NOTHING
#   SHOULD. The directory it sits in is rejected as a source on purpose. And the `notation`
#   below carries a `:fixture:` segment that no query touches -- `contrato-empresarial`
#   already spells the sibling segment `:declaracao:` in the other edition, so the convention
#   has drifted with nothing leaning on it. A URN is an identifier, not a claim.
--
-- The five top-level declarations: pm:processModulus and asrt:composition/dependence/coverage/run.
SELECT s.name AS filing,
       x.root, x.ns,
       fi.notation, fi.absent AS notation_absent,
       f.evidence, f.evidence_absent,
       x.witness, x.observed_at, x.ran_at
FROM      pm.source s
CROSS JOIN XMLTABLE(XMLNAMESPACES('https://example.invalid/assertion/1.0' AS asrt),
       '/*' PASSING s.body
       COLUMNS root        text PATH 'local-name(.)',
               ns          text PATH 'namespace-uri(.)',
               witness     text PATH 'asrt:witness',
               observed_at text PATH 'asrt:observedAt',
               ran_at      text PATH 'asrt:ranAt') x
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(composition/notations.sqlc)
) fi ON fi.filing = s.name
-- ⛔ pm.filing raw, and deliberately: scope/every_filing.sqlc drops evidence_absent, and a
--    document that declines to say what it is evidence FOR is exactly what this relation reports.
LEFT JOIN pm.filing f ON f.name = s.name
